Apply before adding storage, network, or cross-layer calls on tracker ingest or settlement paths. Topology and diagrams: `docs/ARCHITECTURE.md`. Implementation detail: `hot-path.mdc`, `data-layer.mdc`, `cold-path.mdc`. SLAs: `core.mdc`.

## Hot/cold boundary

Hot path: tracker `/track`, `/click`, `/openrtb/bid`, `/tg/*` — accept or reject under SLA; **202 does not mean PG/CH wrote**.

**Forbidden on synchronous hot request path:**

- Postgres, ClickHouse, outbox, sqlc, or any DB driver call
- `internal/fraud` ML inference — read `ml:score:boost:*` snapshot only
- External HTTP/RPC except bounded Redis ops below
- Per-request campaign catalog load from DB — `atomic.Pointer` snapshot + pub/sub reload only
- Outbox or admin mutation handlers on tracker

Cold path: control `:8188`, processor `:8186`, payment, ledger, IVT/fraud workers. PG is financial truth; CH is analytics; config reaches tracker via outbox → Redis → pub/sub.

## I/O round-trips (hot path)

| Invariant | Rule |
| :--- | :--- |
| Sync Redis | **At most one** `EVALSHA` per accepted event (UnifiedFilter). **Zero** when local quanta full-skip eligible |
| Filter order | Go-local filters first (license, geo, schedule, …). **No** Redis between cheap filters. UnifiedFilter **last** |
| Stream log | `XADD` async via StreamProducer/BrokerProducer — **not** in the same Lua script as debit |
| Multi-key atomicity | All campaign keys on one master: `{campaign_id}` hash tag + StaticSlotSharder. **No** Redis Cluster `MOVED` on hot path |
| Admission | `TryReserve` **before** Lua debit — never spend then fail enqueue |
| Post-debit fail | `budget-rollback.lua` + local quanta refund — never orphan debit |
| OpenRTB | In-process `RunAuction` only — **no** full FilterEngine chain on `/openrtb/bid` |
| Registry | No per-event PG/Redis config fetch — snapshot at loop start |

**Banned hot patterns:** sequential Redis round-trips per event; GET-then-SET budget; sync stream write before 202; LISTEN/NOTIFY; message bus publish on `/track` accept path; N filter Redis calls.

Pinned gnet workers must not block on Redis — `FilterEngine.Check` (incl. `EVALSHA`) runs in detached goroutine; copy strings before async response write.

## Memory and correctness (hot path)

- Zero heap allocs on ingest path — `make test-alloc-gate`, `escape_heap_gate.sh`
- No `defer` in inner hot loops; no escaping closures; no `interface{}` / `fmt.Sprintf` on `/track`
- **Fail closed** (503) on infra — never ghost-accept spend without debit + stream reservation aligned
- Budget invariant (cold): `current_spend <= budget_limit` in Postgres — `AssertBudgetInvariant` (±1 micro-unit)

## Cold path invariants

- Admin mutation + `outbox_events` enqueue in **same PG transaction**
- OutboxWorker poll (~20 ms) — **no** outbox on tracker
- No O(N) DB round-trips in loops on changed handlers (`cold_path_static_gate.sh`)
- Processor settles streams → PG/CH; does **not** write `balance_ledger`
- Settlement idempotency via `sync_idempotency`

## Sharding

```
slot  = CRC32C(campaign_id) & 1023
shard = slot_table[slot]
```

Edge Lua (`edge-slot-map.lua`) must match Go. Jump Hash = tests/benches only.

